# Publish remote Windows agent

Mirrored for Antigravity: [`.agents/rules/publish-remote-agent.md`](../../.agents/rules/publish-remote-agent.md)

## When to publish (agents — do not ask)

After you change **`remotes/c_remote_core/**`** or **`remotes/c_remote_windows/**`** (streaming, WebRTC, pair, OTA, capture), and the task is meant for production / the user's VM:

```powershell
.\_\scripts\deploy\publish_remote_agent.ps1
```

Or `publish_app_release.ps1 -RemoteAgent`. Requires repo-root `.env.local` (`YB_PASSWORD`, `DEPLOY_AUTH_TOKEN`, S3/CAS).

End the turn with **Publish summary** per `publish-perf-report.mdc` (`target`: `remote-windows-agent`).

## What publish does

1. `cargo build --release` → OTA zip (Blake3) + Inno Setup installer
2. Upload to CAS → `ai.config` `app.release.c35.remote-windows`
3. NATS `c35.release.remote-windows` (agents download in background)
4. Smoke + prod OTA dry-run scripts (fix smoke if they fail)

## What agents cannot do automatically

| Gap | Who acts |
|-----|----------|
| Install/replace binary **inside** user's VM | User: tray **Update**, or run `AlienAI_Remote_Windows_Setup-*.exe` from [alienai.id/download/agent.exe](https://alienai.id/download/agent.exe) |
| OTA apply while **WebRTC viewer** connected | Agent waits until idle (`active_sessions == 0`); disconnect Remote tab or use in-app **Update** button |
| Bump `agent_version.dart` build | Publish script bumps from `remotes/.../version` or build script — commit if version changed |
| GitHub Actions on every push | Not wired unless a workflow is added |

## VM quick path after publish

1. Paired agent online → NATS push → background download → **Update (vN)** in Devices Remote toolbar when idle.
2. Fresh VM → download installer from `https://alienai.id/download/agent.exe` (Setup), pair, open Remote.
